io: keep only the `_io` re-exports and the seek constants.
Monty has no metaclasses, `abc` or `del` (#1032), and its `_io` has no `_IOBase` classes, `FileIO`, `BufferedRWPair`,
`IncrementalNewlineDecoder` or `_WindowsConsoleIO`, so this drops the `IOBase`/`RawIOBase`/`BufferedIOBase`/`TextIOBase`
ABCs and their `register` calls, the `Reader`/`Writer` protocols and those names, and trims `__all__` to match.
TODO: shrink this patch as those land, and drop it once the unpatched module loads.

